Subject: [PATCH] privatebrowsing: load the Aequera private page stylesheet

Why Firefox source must change:
  about:privatebrowsing is a fixed Firefox page (mapped in C++ by
  AboutRedirector) that names its stylesheets in its own markup; no pref,
  policy, or theme can add one. Aequera keeps the page, its localized
  strings, and its behavior, and only restyles it to match the Aequera new
  tab page.

What it changes (one stylesheet link, last in <head>):
  chrome://browser/content/aequera/privatebrowsing/aequera-private.css
  (overlay "shell-chrome"). The page's CSP already allows chrome: styles.
  Every rule sits inside @media -moz-pref("aequera.privatebrowsing.enabled")
  (the query Firefox's own stylesheet uses for Nova); the pref is absent
  in Firefox, so the page is unchanged there.

Depends on: overlay "shell-chrome" (the stylesheet itself).
Validation: aequera/shell/firefox/tests/browser/browser_aequera_private.js
  (private and normal windows: artwork, search box, and promos hidden,
  Aequera icon tile shown, Firefox's text intact; pref off restores
  Firefox's design); Firefox's about:privatebrowsing tests with the pref off.
Upstream risk: low for the patch (one line in <head>); the stylesheet
  targets Firefox's class names, which the test covers.

diff --git a/browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html b/browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html
index c5ba88b544ea..dd97733aadf8 100644
--- a/browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html
+++ b/browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html
@@ -24,6 +24,11 @@
       href="chrome://browser/skin/privatebrowsing/aboutPrivateBrowsing.css"
       media="all"
     />
+    <link
+      rel="stylesheet"
+      href="chrome://browser/content/aequera/privatebrowsing/aequera-private.css"
+      media="all"
+    />
     <link rel="localization" href="branding/brand.ftl" />
     <link rel="localization" href="toolkit/branding/brandings.ftl" />
     <link rel="localization" href="toolkit/global/mozPromo.ftl" />
